 "result": "The session round-trips these types by tagging them: each non-JSON type is wrapped in a single-key dict like `{\" t\": [...]}` on the way out and unwrapped on the way back.\n\n**Classes (all in `src/tessel/json/tag.py`):**\n- `TypedCookieSerializer` (`:219`) is the serializer. `tag()` (`:289`) walks a value, and the first registered tag whose `check()` matches wraps it. `untag()` (`:297`) reverses that. `dumps()` (`:321`) and `loads()` (`:325`) do `tag` plus JSON encode, and JSON decode plus `untag`.\n- `TypeMarker` (`:73`) is the base class for tags. It defines `check`, `to_json`, `to_python` and `tag`, and each tag has a short `key`.\n- Concrete tags:\n  - `TagTuple` (`:133`) stores a tuple as a list.\n  - `TagBytes` (`:159`) stores bytes as base64.\n  - `TagDateTime` (`:205`) stores a datetime as an HTTP date string.\n  - `TagDict` (`:93`) escapes user dicts that happen to look like a tag.\n  - There are also `TagMarkup`, `TagUUID` and a tag for a plain dict.\n\n**Session wiring:**\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:273` creates the module-level `session_json_serializer = TypedCookieSerializer()`.\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:300` sets it as `serializer` on the cookie session interface.\n- `src/tessel/sessions.py:316` passes it as `serializer=` when building the signing serializer for the cookie.",
